Functions:
1. Name: listAllBreeds
Description: Returns all available dog breeds, including their sub-breeds.
Input: None
Output: A JSON object containing all available dog breeds and their sub-breeds. Each key represents a breed, and its value is an array of sub-breeds. Example: {"affenpinscher": [], "african": [], "airedale": [], ...}

2. Name: randomImage
Description: Shows a random image of a dog of a specific breed.
Input: Required. String. The breed name. Example: {"breed": "golden"}
Output: A JSON object containing the URL of the random image. Example: {"message": "https://images.dog.ceo/breeds/golden/n02099601_100.jpg", "status": "success"}

3. Name: multipleImages
Description: Generates multiple images of a specific breed.
Input: Required. String. The breed name. Optional. Integer. The number of images to generate (default is 1). Example: {"breed": "golden", "count": 3}
Output: A JSON object containing an array of URLs of the generated images. Example: {"message": ["https://images.dog.ceo/breeds/golden/n02099601_100.jpg", "https://images.dog.ceo/breeds/golden/n02099601_101.jpg", "https://images.dog.ceo/breeds/golden/n02099601_102.jpg"], "status": "success"}

4. Name: subBreedList
Description: Returns all sub-breeds of a specific breed.
Input: Required. String. The breed name. Example: {"breed": "golden"}
Output: A JSON object containing an array of sub-breeds. Example: {"message": ["english", "american"], "status": "success"}

5. Name: search
Description: Allows users to search for a specific breed by its name.
Input: Required. String. The breed name to search for. Example: {"q": "golden"}
Output: A JSON object containing an array of matching breed names. Example: {"message": ["golden", "goldenretriever"], "status": "success"}

